Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:30:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Reorganize the setup menu

The setup menu grew a card at a time, and some cards had become a mix:
Hardware > Graphics held the Intel and the NVIDIA GPU, the display at
wake and the Intel display audio, General > Advanced the NMIs and the
ACPI processor objects, and the options for macOS were spread over
three categories. Reorganize it into six categories, by what the user
looks for:

- General: About this ThinkPad, Boot, Sound;
- Energy Saver: Battery, Processor, Processor voltage (the undervolting
  options of drivers/intel/oc_mailbox, a category of their own until
  now), Thermal, Power;
- Hardware: Intel graphics, NVIDIA graphics, Storage (the SATA ports),
  Expansion ports (ExpressCard and Thunderbolt), Wireless;
- Keyboard: Keys, Pointing devices;
- Security: Flash protection, Memory protection, Virtualization,
  Management Engine;
- Compatibility, new: macOS, with the options that take the place of
  parts of an OpenCore configuration (ACPI processor objects, C-state
  configuration lock, NVIDIA GPU off under macOS, Light the display up
  at wake, Intel display audio) and a note on the slot switches;
  Advanced, with the non-maskable interrupts.

Each option is in one card only. The option names, values and defaults
do not change, so the saved settings stay. The help of each option of
the mainboard says what it does, its default and when to change it, as
the help of the options of the CPU, the northbridge, Lynx Point and the
EC now does.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init. The
setup of both, in QEMU with the CFR record of the W541, has the six
categories with the cards above; every option is in one card only.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
